# NL Eats environment variables (copy to `.env.local`; never commit real secrets).
#
# ALL of these are SERVER-ONLY. Do NOT prefix any with NEXT_PUBLIC_, which would
# inline the value into the client bundle.

# ── Data source ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Leave BOTH unset in development → the app reads the local seed file
# `data/graph-data.csv`. Set BOTH to switch to the Google Sheet published-CSV
# export (free; no API key, no billing) with zero code changes.
#
# GOOGLE_SHEET_ID  = the spreadsheet's document id (the long id in its URL:
#                    https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/<THIS>/edit)
#                    Share the sheet "Anyone with the link → Viewer".
# GOOGLE_SHEET_GID = the specific tab's gid (the `gid=` value in the tab URL; the
#                    first tab is usually 0).
GOOGLE_SHEET_ID=
GOOGLE_SHEET_GID=

# ── Auth gate ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The gate is INERT until BOTH are set: with them unset the site is fully open
# (dev / CI / Netlify preview keep working). Set both in Netlify to raise the wall.
#
# SITE_PASSWORD = shared password checked server-side (constant-time compare).
# AUTH_SECRET   = random key used to HMAC-sign the auth cookie (NOT the password).
#                 Generate one with:  openssl rand -base64 32
SITE_PASSWORD=
AUTH_SECRET=
